    "title": "Gastonia textile company to shut down Davidson County manufacturing plant - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Doug Coats No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nGASTONIA, N.C. (QUEEN CITY NEWS) — A Gastonia-based textile company is shutting down one of its manufacturing facilities in central North Carolina.\nAccording to the N.C. Department of Commerce, Parkdale Mills’ Lexington location is set to close in June, affecting 68 people.\nThe state reports that the plant’s employees were notified of the news April 9.\nParkdale has been in operation since 1916 and touts itself as as the world’s leading manufacturer of spun yarns. Its headquarters is off of South New Hope Road in Gastonia.\nThere are eight other manufacturing or distribution locations in North Carolina.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
    "summary": ", GASTONIA, N.C. (QUEEN CITY NEWS) — A Gastonia-based textile company is shutting down one of its manufacturing facilities in central North Carolina. According to the N.C. Department of Commerce, Parkdale Mills’ Lexington location is set to close in June, affecting 68 people. The state reports that the plant’s employees were notified of the news April 9. Parkdale has been in operation since 1916 and touts itself as as the world’s leading manufacturer of spun yarns. Its headquarters is off of South New Hope Road in Gastonia.",
